{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T15:47:19.037Z","data":{"text":"Task 2 is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Routed every report event-stream and planning-log read through the shared reader**\n- `report.ts`: `getMetricsReport` now wraps an unexported `buildMetricsReport` in `withStreamReads`, so one report run is one read scope. All reads (`projectMeasuredTasks`, `readFirstTaskStartMs`, `readArchivedAtMs`, `hasRejectedEvent`, `collectDeadOutcomes`, the task loop, the folder scan) go through `readEventStream`.\n- `report-dependencies.ts`, `approval-flags.ts`, `planning-economics.ts`, `report-mutation.ts`: their private stream scans use `readEventStream`.\n- `planning-records.ts`: `readPlanRecords` uses `readParsedFile(getPlanLogPath(...), parsePlanRecords)`.\n- `queue-report-detail.ts`: `archivedEventMs` uses `readEventStream` and keeps first-valid-`archived` semantics.\n\n**Tests**\n- Updated the `function-budget.test.ts` grandfather key to `buildMetricsReport`.\n- Added `tests/report-reads-once.test.ts`: asserts no `.jsonl` is read twice, every archived stream (and rejected change stream) is read once, a second call re-reads and counts an appended `tokens` line, and only the allowed modules call `parseEventLines`.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/report-reads-once.test.ts`: passes.\n- Proposal verify `pnpm verify`: passes (exit 0), including the `fixture/report/expected.json` golden and the report text/JSON tests. One intermediate run hit a transient `EADDRINUSE` in `tests/serve.test.ts`; it passes in isolation and on the clean re-run.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/132-report-reads-once/.run/results/2.md`."}}
